WEBVTT

00:09.009 --> 00:10.468
[dramatic music playing]

00:17.726 --> 00:19.519
HONG MIN-BEOM

00:19.602 --> 00:20.770
Hello?

00:20.854 --> 00:22.647
[Gang-yong]
Yeah, I'll be there in ten minutes.

00:22.731 --> 00:24.983
Director Hong, don't hang up the phone.

00:25.525 --> 00:27.193
Just flip it over
and leave it on the table,

00:27.277 --> 00:28.111
so I can listen in.

00:28.194 --> 00:30.447
- [distressed breathing]
- You get what I'm saying, right?

00:33.950 --> 00:34.784
[door closes]

00:36.953 --> 00:37.787
[exhales deeply]

00:39.330 --> 00:40.749
Let me cut to the chase.

00:42.876 --> 00:44.169
[spluttering] What are you doing?

00:44.252 --> 00:46.254
[screams, groaning]

00:46.337 --> 00:47.172
[screaming]

00:49.674 --> 00:51.926
- Stop being a little bitch and sit still.
- [groaning]

00:52.010 --> 00:53.178
GANG-YONG

00:53.261 --> 00:54.095
You there?

00:54.179 --> 00:56.431
I'm right here, asshole.
What the hell are you trying to do?

00:56.514 --> 00:57.932
Do you have a death wish?

00:58.016 --> 00:59.350
- [bones cracking]
- [screams]

00:59.434 --> 01:02.729
You're making a big fucking mistake
right now, you stupid fucking asshole.

01:02.812 --> 01:05.273
- You might want to tell him to shut up.
- [screams]

01:05.356 --> 01:07.609
Dude! Stop!

01:07.692 --> 01:09.819
You're going to rot in a cell
for the rest of your life.

01:09.903 --> 01:10.779
You motherfucker!

01:10.862 --> 01:12.322
[groans]

01:12.405 --> 01:14.949
Fuck! Shut the hell up,
you fucking son of a bitch!

01:17.702 --> 01:19.120
[scoffs] Jackass.

01:21.372 --> 01:22.832
Have you calmed down?

01:25.627 --> 01:26.669
I can't hear you.

01:26.753 --> 01:27.796
[sighs]

01:27.879 --> 01:29.005
Tell me what you want.

01:29.589 --> 01:32.967
There's a report that came into
the Yeongmoonpo Police Department.

01:33.051 --> 01:34.385
In a parking lot,

01:34.469 --> 01:37.347
a guy on a motorcycle slashed a man's neck
and then got away.

01:38.014 --> 01:39.057
Write this.

01:39.808 --> 01:44.479
Seoul, Gangdong, A 6438.

01:45.146 --> 01:47.649
No need to look it up.
It's a fake license plate.

01:48.525 --> 01:50.527
Find out where
the guy on this motorcycle is hiding.

01:50.610 --> 01:51.569
[scoffs]

01:52.320 --> 01:55.365
- Do you know how hard it is--
- [Myeong-gil] I know it takes a long time.

01:56.032 --> 01:57.242
That's why you'll do it.

01:58.118 --> 02:00.453
It's 10:00 right now.
I'll give you five hours.

02:00.537 --> 02:01.830
If you can't find him…

02:01.913 --> 02:03.373
- [bones crack]
- [groans]

02:03.456 --> 02:06.251
…your cousin's little striptease
will be online.

02:06.334 --> 02:09.045
Try to pull something on me,
and it'll also find its way online.

02:09.129 --> 02:11.965
If you don't want to see
lil Group's stock prices tank,

02:12.048 --> 02:13.258
I suggest you do well.

02:13.341 --> 02:14.175
Good luck.

02:15.718 --> 02:16.594
[exhales deeply]

02:18.596 --> 02:19.430
What is it?

02:19.514 --> 02:21.933
[groans] 735629.

02:25.687 --> 02:27.313
[groaning]

02:29.357 --> 02:30.233
See you soon.

02:34.070 --> 02:34.904
[door closes]

02:34.988 --> 02:36.156
Fuck you!

02:36.656 --> 02:38.658
[heavy breathing]

02:40.743 --> 02:42.745
[theme music playing]

03:07.020 --> 03:10.190
BLOODHOUNDS

03:13.359 --> 03:14.819
[distant sirens wailing]

03:17.113 --> 03:18.072
[man 1] Hello, sir.

03:18.156 --> 03:20.074
- [Gang-yong] Whoa, salute!
- [man 2] Salute!

03:20.158 --> 03:23.328
[Gang-yong laughing]
Soju's on me. I'm buying.

03:30.585 --> 03:32.629
- [man 2] This way, sir.
- [Gang-yong] Right, thank you.

03:32.712 --> 03:33.963
- [man 3] Sir.
- [Gang-yong] Hello.

03:37.050 --> 03:40.011
[Yang-jung] They boil the bodies for days
until the bones get soft.

03:40.094 --> 03:42.430
They grind them up
and pour them into the ocean.

03:42.513 --> 03:44.557
It costs 15 million to do all that.

03:44.641 --> 03:46.184
You couldn't find a bone.

03:46.976 --> 03:49.145
Turning people into stew. Sick fucks.

03:49.771 --> 03:50.730
Who told you that?

03:51.606 --> 03:52.982
I visited Seung-deok in prison.

03:53.066 --> 03:55.193
How does that punk know this
when he's locked up?

03:55.276 --> 03:57.862
[Yang-jung] Prison is the best source
for information like this.

03:59.280 --> 04:00.907
[Du-yeong] You guys all right back there?

04:01.449 --> 04:02.992
- Yes, sir.
- Yes. We're all right, sir.

04:03.076 --> 04:05.536
Seeing all that couldn't have been easy.

04:06.871 --> 04:07.705
[Du-yeong sighs]

04:07.789 --> 04:11.626
By the way, what will happen
when they open the casino?

04:11.709 --> 04:12.710
What will happen?

04:13.836 --> 04:15.588
Kim Myeong-gil will make lots of money.

04:15.672 --> 04:17.006
- Oh.
- [Du-yeong] Gun-woo.

04:17.507 --> 04:18.341
Sir.

04:18.424 --> 04:22.428
Gambling and drug addicts
take out a lot of private loans.

04:22.512 --> 04:25.556
Kim Myeong-gil connects the casino
with moneylending.

04:26.057 --> 04:30.061
The more people visit his casino,
the more people will take out loans.

04:30.561 --> 04:32.981
He'll just rake in easy money day by day.

04:33.940 --> 04:35.984
But I thought
only foreigners could go to casinos.

04:36.651 --> 04:38.820
Do you think
Kim Myeong-gil cares about the law?

04:38.903 --> 04:41.489
He'll let all the big spenders in
through the back door.

04:41.572 --> 04:44.242
They're not going to make any money
operating legally.

04:44.742 --> 04:47.370
[sighs] Once he's made enough money,

04:47.453 --> 04:49.289
Kim Myeong-gil will buy a building
with a loan.

04:49.372 --> 04:53.668
Then he'll use that building as collateral
for another loan to buy a bigger building.

04:53.751 --> 04:54.627
Man.

04:55.128 --> 04:56.713
That asshole's a real piece of work.

04:56.796 --> 05:00.258
He'll go even harder running the casino
to pay back that loan.

05:00.341 --> 05:03.177
And Smile Capital will squeeze
even more people dry.

05:03.261 --> 05:06.055
[Yang-jung] It'll be the opening
of Kim Myeong-gil's personal kingdom.

05:06.139 --> 05:07.432
[ominous music playing]

05:11.686 --> 05:12.520
[music ends]

05:18.192 --> 05:22.739
The money Myeong-gil stole from me
back then was worth over 20 billion won

05:22.822 --> 05:23.781
at the time.

05:23.865 --> 05:25.408
Once we get it back,

05:25.491 --> 05:27.869
how would you feel
about taking a trip around the world

05:27.952 --> 05:29.829
with Gun-woo and Woo-jin, huh?

05:30.955 --> 05:33.082
We have enough money as it is.

05:35.084 --> 05:36.002
That's true.

05:36.919 --> 05:38.755
And we can't travel because of COVID

05:40.798 --> 05:41.632
True.

05:43.343 --> 05:44.635
Why don't we go to Rome together?

05:47.555 --> 05:48.556
Why Rome?

05:48.639 --> 05:52.101
When I was 20,
I watched a film called Roman Holiday.

05:53.019 --> 05:56.105
Back then, I vowed to go one day
when I made a lot of money,

05:56.189 --> 05:57.857
but I haven't had the chance yet.

05:58.441 --> 06:02.111
I thought it might be nice
to go with you all,

06:02.195 --> 06:03.446
the three of you, you know?

06:04.655 --> 06:05.531
[exhales sharply]

06:07.492 --> 06:09.827
If we go,
I'll buy you guys anything you want.

06:10.912 --> 06:14.040
Grandpa, Italy is way too expensive.

06:14.123 --> 06:15.541
It's the land of luxury.

06:16.125 --> 06:18.711
Look, kid, I'm Choi Tae-ho, all right?

06:19.796 --> 06:21.672
I'll show you how to really spend money.

06:22.256 --> 06:23.091
[chuckles]

06:23.716 --> 06:26.803
Grandpa, that's called "flexing," okay?

06:27.970 --> 06:31.474
Yeah, well, I'll show you flexing.
I'll do some big flexing.

06:31.557 --> 06:32.475
[laughing]

06:32.558 --> 06:35.269
Not big flexing. You just say "flex."

06:38.064 --> 06:38.940
Flex.

06:39.023 --> 06:41.109
[laughing]

06:41.192 --> 06:42.360
[chuckles]

06:44.404 --> 06:48.282
So when this is over,
we'll all go together, okay?

06:49.742 --> 06:51.077
[Mr. Choi chuckles]

06:51.619 --> 06:52.995
[soft piano music playing]

06:58.126 --> 06:59.335
[laughing]

06:59.419 --> 07:00.670
[laughing]

07:03.339 --> 07:04.215
[cell phone vibrating]

07:04.757 --> 07:05.591
Hello, sir.

07:06.884 --> 07:08.302
That sounds good, sir.

07:09.345 --> 07:10.179
Yes.

07:11.264 --> 07:14.392
Hm. Mr. Choi invited us
for drinks at his place.

07:16.519 --> 07:18.271
I guess he's in a pretty good mood.

07:19.605 --> 07:20.940
Hey, you guys drink?

07:21.941 --> 07:22.900
You know it!

07:31.993 --> 07:33.327
[tense music playing]

08:06.486 --> 08:07.612
[sighs]

08:17.914 --> 08:19.081
Can we speed it up a little?

08:19.165 --> 08:21.375
There's double
and quadruple-speed playback. Which one?

08:21.459 --> 08:23.252
- Let's make it double.
- Got it.

08:30.092 --> 08:32.053
If I was Kim Myeong-gil,

08:32.136 --> 08:35.681
I would've thought to move the hard drive
to a safer location by now,

08:35.765 --> 08:38.434
just in case
Im Jang-do revealed my weaknesses.

08:39.227 --> 08:41.771
[exhales] Do you think he can afford that?

08:42.522 --> 08:43.981
We've boxed him into a corner.

08:44.982 --> 08:48.319
He has no one left to help him now
except for that Mr. Jung guy.

08:49.362 --> 08:50.238
Besides,

08:51.155 --> 08:54.116
I don't think that
Kim Myeong-gil would trust just anyone.

08:55.368 --> 08:57.036
He doesn't have to move it far.

08:57.119 --> 08:59.413
He could hide it in the trunk of a car,
and we wouldn't find it.

08:59.497 --> 09:01.541
- [Gun-woo] Hm.
- [Yang-jung] Kim Myeong-gil knows that.

09:02.250 --> 09:03.292
[Du-yeong] You're right.

09:03.918 --> 09:05.878
The tides would turn in our favor

09:05.962 --> 09:08.798
if we manage to recruit an enemy of his
over to our side.

09:09.799 --> 09:11.467
[breathes deeply]

09:11.551 --> 09:13.970
But to do that, we need the hard drive.

09:14.053 --> 09:17.598
It should contain everything
about Myeong-gil's blackmail victims.

09:18.099 --> 09:20.643
Those people share our motivations.

09:21.394 --> 09:24.146
[inhales sharply]
And there will be many powerful people,

09:24.230 --> 09:26.399
like the heir of the Iil Group
mixed in with the bunch.

09:27.483 --> 09:29.026
[Mr. Choi inhales sharply, exhales]

09:29.110 --> 09:31.821
The longer this fight drags on,
the less likely we'll come out on top.

09:32.488 --> 09:35.741
I'm sure Myeong-gil has made
a vast network of connections by now.

09:36.367 --> 09:39.245
Every cop, prosecutor, and politician
that could be bought

09:39.328 --> 09:42.039
is probably in his pocket by now.

09:42.665 --> 09:45.668
We can't ever let our guard down,
or else we're finished.

09:46.544 --> 09:47.545
Yeah.

09:48.129 --> 09:51.173
But it's true we've taken down
three of his thugs, right?

09:51.841 --> 09:52.675
[grunts]

09:53.593 --> 09:56.262
It makes sense that we get anxious
when looking at the big picture,

09:56.887 --> 09:59.599
but the way I see it,
I think we're doing pretty well.

09:59.682 --> 10:01.225
I mean, no one's gotten hurt so far.

10:01.892 --> 10:02.727
That's true.

10:03.561 --> 10:05.271
[Hyeon-ju]
Let's take things one at a time.

10:05.354 --> 10:08.274
We can take Kim Myeong-gil down
and then his company.

10:08.899 --> 10:12.153
Besides, now that Im Jang-do
and Kim Jun-min's out of the picture,

10:12.236 --> 10:14.530
Kim Myeong-gil must be feeling
the noose tighten.

10:15.573 --> 10:16.657
[inhales deeply]

10:17.158 --> 10:18.951
I guess she does have a point.

10:19.035 --> 10:20.286
[chuckles softly]

10:20.828 --> 10:22.163
Mm…

10:22.663 --> 10:23.497
[Woo-jin grunts]

10:25.041 --> 10:26.792
[Woo-jin] Ah, yes, um,

10:26.876 --> 10:28.461
Mr. Choi, sirs.

10:31.547 --> 10:36.135
I would like to propose a toast
for everyone's safety and our shared goal.

10:37.470 --> 10:40.014
When I say, "Find that hard drive
we will do,"

10:40.097 --> 10:42.266
then you say,
"Kim Myeong-gil, you are through."

10:42.350 --> 10:43.684
[all laughing]

10:43.768 --> 10:45.686
I'd appreciate it if you said it loud.

10:45.770 --> 10:47.355
Let's get started. Raise your glasses.

10:49.398 --> 10:51.108
Find that hard drive, yes we do.

10:51.192 --> 10:53.694
- Kim Myeong-gil.
- [all] You are through!

10:54.612 --> 10:55.863
[gentle piano music playing]

11:06.666 --> 11:09.794
[inaudible dialogue]

11:31.440 --> 11:32.608
[inaudible dialogue]

11:44.662 --> 11:46.956
[Gang-yong] I'm on my way over
to Joongang Police Station.

11:47.039 --> 11:49.250
Those assholes moved
from Dongpa-gu to Joongang-gu.

11:50.084 --> 11:51.419
Can you find them by 3:00?

11:52.837 --> 11:55.381
I'll find them soon
if they stopped in Joongang-gu,

11:55.464 --> 11:58.551
but if they crossed over,
I'll have to keep looking, I guess.

12:00.344 --> 12:01.512
Please, bro.

12:01.595 --> 12:03.097
Don't worry about it.

12:03.180 --> 12:05.725
We'll do what the bastard wants for now.

12:06.767 --> 12:09.979
Once we make it past this,
I'll think of a way to fuck this guy up.

12:11.021 --> 12:12.231
Thank you. Seriously.

12:12.314 --> 12:13.607
[Gang-yong] Min-beom,

12:13.691 --> 12:16.944
you think I'd just let some asshole
mess with my family like this?

12:17.570 --> 12:18.404
It'll be fine.

12:18.487 --> 12:19.447
Okay?

12:19.530 --> 12:20.948
You're all I have right now.

12:22.074 --> 12:23.993
Don't drink too much, okay?

12:24.910 --> 12:25.786
Mm.

12:25.870 --> 12:26.912
[sniffles]

12:29.039 --> 12:30.207
[exhales deeply]

12:32.126 --> 12:33.586
[Woo-jin groaning]

12:34.086 --> 12:35.838
[Gun-woo grunts] Jeez.

12:35.921 --> 12:37.006
[Gun-woo sighs]

12:39.049 --> 12:41.051
- [Woo-jin groaning]
- [Gun-woo grunting]

12:44.555 --> 12:45.556
[exhales deeply]

12:46.515 --> 12:49.226
Why did he drink so much
if he's such a lightweight?

12:49.310 --> 12:50.352
[Gun-woo grunts]

12:51.187 --> 12:53.355
[Gun-woo] I guess
he was in a pretty good mood today.

12:53.439 --> 12:54.815
I'm going to bed. What about you?

12:54.899 --> 12:56.400
I'm going to head back downstairs.

12:56.484 --> 12:58.235
- Aren't you tired?
- Not really.

12:59.236 --> 13:00.237
[Hyeon-ju grunts]

13:01.947 --> 13:02.782
Good work today.

13:02.865 --> 13:03.824
Yeah.

13:06.243 --> 13:08.746
[snoring softly]

13:10.122 --> 13:10.956
[So-yeon] Gun-woo.

13:12.374 --> 13:13.417
Gun-woo?

13:15.336 --> 13:16.253
You're not asleep?

13:17.379 --> 13:18.923
No, why are you awake?

13:19.006 --> 13:21.008
Oh, everyone is downstairs having a drink.

13:21.091 --> 13:22.343
You're drinking too?

13:22.426 --> 13:23.928
Mm-mm. Not me.

13:24.011 --> 13:24.887
Good.

13:26.680 --> 13:28.933
I guess I'll make hangover soup
in the morning.

13:29.016 --> 13:30.935
Great. Get some sleep.
I'll close the door.

13:31.018 --> 13:32.561
Okay, sleep tight.

13:32.645 --> 13:33.813
Good night, Mom.

13:36.106 --> 13:39.068
God, it's been so long
since we drank together.

13:40.986 --> 13:41.946
Mm.

13:42.029 --> 13:43.155
[cell phone vibrating]

13:45.199 --> 13:46.867
[Du-yeong grunting]

13:50.079 --> 13:51.413
[Du-yeong exhales deeply]

13:58.337 --> 13:59.171
Is it a woman?

13:59.755 --> 14:02.925
- [grunts softly]
- Who would call you this late at night?

14:07.221 --> 14:08.138
Tell me.

14:10.766 --> 14:11.600
Hey…

14:14.478 --> 14:15.813
I'm going to be a dad.

14:17.523 --> 14:18.524
When?

14:19.108 --> 14:21.902
In two months. It's a girl. [laughs]

14:21.986 --> 14:23.070
[inhales sharply]

14:23.571 --> 14:25.698
We've been together for three years now.

14:26.657 --> 14:30.077
Hey, man, if you had family,
you should've told me, you idiot.

14:30.160 --> 14:32.329
Then you would've told me not to come.

14:36.584 --> 14:38.502
Go home now. I'll wrap things up here.

14:38.586 --> 14:40.963
It's been so long
since we had a drink together.

14:41.046 --> 14:42.131
I want to stay.

14:42.214 --> 14:43.632
I said go home.

14:44.550 --> 14:46.093
Oh, don't be mad.

14:49.054 --> 14:49.889
Here.

14:50.931 --> 14:51.807
No, I'm good.

14:52.850 --> 14:55.352
It's not for you. Get your wife some meat.

14:55.436 --> 14:57.980
She needs iron right now. Come on.

15:00.608 --> 15:01.817
It's too much.

15:05.029 --> 15:06.113
Aren't you coming downstairs?

15:06.780 --> 15:07.781
Yeah, I'm coming.

15:07.865 --> 15:09.491
- [Gun-woo] I'll go on ahead.
- Sure.

15:11.994 --> 15:13.078
Call a cab.

15:13.162 --> 15:15.414
I'll have another smoke
until it gets here.

15:17.374 --> 15:18.208
Hey.

15:21.795 --> 15:22.630
Thank you.

15:24.048 --> 15:25.341
Don't make it weird.

15:27.718 --> 15:30.638
[inhales sharply]
You're the best, you know?

15:31.138 --> 15:33.390
I'm going to get some hanwoo
on my way back.

15:37.311 --> 15:38.646
- [exhales]
- [Mr. Choi] Oh.

15:38.729 --> 15:40.731
Hyeon-ju says she's going to bed early.

15:40.814 --> 15:41.649
Hm.

15:44.109 --> 15:45.027
Are you all right?

15:45.736 --> 15:46.570
Yes.

15:49.198 --> 15:50.032
[exhales deeply]

15:53.827 --> 15:55.496
You seem really worried right now, sir.

15:56.163 --> 15:59.291
I'm the one who taught Myeong-gil.
He's my responsibility.

16:00.250 --> 16:03.837
But when my body… broke down,

16:05.839 --> 16:07.091
I couldn't fight him.

16:09.176 --> 16:10.302
The only thing

16:11.887 --> 16:14.473
that I could manage
was taking care of Hyeon-ju.

16:18.560 --> 16:20.729
[breathes deeply]

16:22.940 --> 16:24.942
[dramatic music playing]

16:30.823 --> 16:32.116
[inhales deeply]

16:32.908 --> 16:33.993
[exhales deeply]

17:25.669 --> 17:26.795
Who are you?

17:27.713 --> 17:28.589
Oh, I--

17:29.631 --> 17:30.507
I'm a friend

17:32.259 --> 17:33.635
of your father's.

17:34.845 --> 17:35.804
[crying]

17:38.682 --> 17:41.351
Oh no. Don't cry. Don't cry.

17:41.435 --> 17:43.645
[crying]

17:43.729 --> 17:44.688
Hey.

17:46.982 --> 17:47.900
Papa!

17:49.651 --> 17:51.737
[crying continues]

17:53.280 --> 17:56.617
CONDOLENCES

17:58.285 --> 17:59.411
[man] Sorry for your loss.

18:00.871 --> 18:02.831
[Mr. Choi]
Get the best condolence flowers you can,

18:02.915 --> 18:05.042
then fill up the room with them.

18:05.125 --> 18:05.959
[Yang-jung] Yes, sir.

18:06.043 --> 18:07.377
Have ten men guard the place

18:07.461 --> 18:09.546
until they're done moving the coffin
to the grave site.

18:10.255 --> 18:12.049
- Should we arm them?
- Uh, no.

18:12.549 --> 18:14.843
It's for the child.
She's doing the wake alone.

18:14.927 --> 18:16.178
And let's get her some food.

18:16.261 --> 18:17.221
Yes, sir.

18:18.597 --> 18:21.391
Sir, I think you left your scarf inside.

18:21.475 --> 18:22.768
Oh, don't worry about it.

18:24.103 --> 18:25.312
[sighs]

18:25.395 --> 18:27.397
Why on earth did he kill himself?

18:28.023 --> 18:30.984
He delivered papers in the morning,
made parts at a factory,

18:31.068 --> 18:32.778
and worked as a chauffeur at night.

18:32.861 --> 18:35.155
He got just three hours of sleep every day

18:35.239 --> 18:37.991
for two years working graveyard shifts
to save his daughter.

18:38.075 --> 18:40.828
Then his child gets better,
and he kills himself?

18:41.703 --> 18:42.788
I just don't get it.

18:43.664 --> 18:45.666
I told him
that I didn't need any interest.

18:45.749 --> 18:47.876
He just had to pay back the principal,

18:47.960 --> 18:50.921
and I'd give him an extension
if he ever needed more time.

18:58.428 --> 19:00.347
Um, I'll look into it.

19:00.931 --> 19:02.307
I just don't understand.

19:10.524 --> 19:11.400
Here.

19:15.946 --> 19:16.864
Third floor.

19:25.914 --> 19:26.874
Excuse me.

19:29.126 --> 19:29.960
Jesus.

19:30.544 --> 19:33.505
Are you, by chance, on your way
to Mr. Cha Sang-ho's funeral?

19:35.174 --> 19:36.008
Yes.

19:39.678 --> 19:43.557
Two years ago, when I got surgery
and couldn't lift things,

19:44.057 --> 19:48.520
Hyeon-ju's dad would take out the trash
for me for three months.

19:49.855 --> 19:54.610
God, he was the nicest,
hardest-working person around.

19:55.944 --> 19:57.738
I felt so bad for Hyeon-ju.

19:58.238 --> 20:01.450
That poor little thing sick
without a mother around.

20:02.034 --> 20:04.953
I used to feed her
and fill up their fridge,

20:05.454 --> 20:07.206
so they didn't run out things to eat.

20:07.289 --> 20:11.168
Why would he kill himself
now that Hyeon-ju has gotten better?

20:11.251 --> 20:14.421
It's because of the loan shark bastards!

20:15.130 --> 20:17.257
They used to come over
whenever they pleased,

20:18.258 --> 20:22.054
grabbing him by the neck
and beating him. God--

20:22.137 --> 20:23.096
What did they look like?

20:24.056 --> 20:27.893
Uh, well,
one was almost the size of a brown bear.

20:28.393 --> 20:31.104
The other one was tall, incredibly tall.

20:34.107 --> 20:35.359
[Mr. Choi] One month later,

20:35.984 --> 20:39.196
another person I had lent money to
killed themselves.

20:40.072 --> 20:42.824
It was also someone
I had given an interest-free loan

20:42.908 --> 20:44.743
because of a sick family member.

20:46.161 --> 20:48.330
- I'm going home too soon.
- [grunting]

20:48.413 --> 20:50.082
[Du-yeong laughing]

20:50.165 --> 20:51.291
[Yang-jung] Watch the stairs.

20:53.460 --> 20:54.711
[Du-yeong exhales deeply]

20:55.545 --> 20:56.880
[Du-yeong] Ah, my brother.

20:58.423 --> 20:59.383
[Du-yeong grunts]

21:03.220 --> 21:04.096
I'll go now.

21:05.555 --> 21:07.224
- Get home safe.
- Okay.

21:09.059 --> 21:10.060
Good night.

21:16.358 --> 21:18.026
[Mr. Choi] Yang-jung found out later

21:18.777 --> 21:21.113
that the people
that I had given those loans

21:21.196 --> 21:23.365
for their family's medical expenses

21:25.367 --> 21:27.411
had been visited by Myeong-gil.

21:27.494 --> 21:29.871
He was going around taking several million

21:29.955 --> 21:31.915
in loan extension fees from them
every month,

21:33.375 --> 21:35.711
telling them
that he was following my orders.

21:37.004 --> 21:40.215
My mom fell for the same trick.

21:41.842 --> 21:44.177
He hid a clause in the fine print
within the contract.

21:47.139 --> 21:48.098
[Mr. Choi] Oh.

21:49.850 --> 21:51.143
I'm so sorry.

21:51.226 --> 21:52.352
[exhales]

21:53.812 --> 21:55.856
A lot of people got hurt because of me.

21:56.648 --> 21:57.649
That's not true.

21:58.650 --> 22:01.320
You don't need to feel sorry
for what happened to us, Mr. Choi.

22:02.029 --> 22:05.365
I think you have a strong sense
of responsibility,

22:05.449 --> 22:07.284
which is why you feel so much guilt.

22:08.035 --> 22:10.746
Those who are truly shameless
feel no guilt whatsoever.

22:11.455 --> 22:15.000
They always blame others
and prey on people weaker than them.

22:16.335 --> 22:17.210
[inhales sharply]

22:17.294 --> 22:19.755
But I think the only reason
why we're all gathered here today

22:19.838 --> 22:22.215
is because of the goodwill you've spread
throughout the years.

22:22.799 --> 22:27.429
I don't think Hyeon-ju knows
that you bought the orphanage for her,

22:28.597 --> 22:30.223
but I'm sure
she will always believe in you

22:30.307 --> 22:31.433
with all her heart.

22:32.017 --> 22:32.851
We'll work together

22:32.934 --> 22:35.103
and bring Kim Myeong-gil down
no matter what.

22:35.687 --> 22:37.314
So please stop blaming yourself,

22:39.191 --> 22:41.276
and please take care of your health, sir.

22:46.823 --> 22:47.949
[Mr. Choi exhales]

22:51.495 --> 22:52.871
[breathes deeply]

22:55.624 --> 22:59.544
When we're done, I'll set you up
with your own private boxing gym.

23:00.045 --> 23:01.755
That should help you focus
on your training

23:01.838 --> 23:04.049
until you eventually become a champion.

23:04.674 --> 23:08.845
And I'll build a nice big café
for your mom on the ground floor.

23:10.013 --> 23:12.057
No rent until the day I die.

23:13.517 --> 23:14.351
Wow.

23:14.434 --> 23:15.727
[shaky breathing]

23:16.520 --> 23:17.729
[whimpers]

23:17.813 --> 23:20.273
What, you don't know what to say
all of a sudden?

23:20.357 --> 23:21.191
No.

23:23.360 --> 23:24.736
A thank you would do.

23:26.154 --> 23:26.988
Oh.

23:28.115 --> 23:29.533
Thank you so much, Mr. Choi.

23:29.616 --> 23:30.534
No.

23:32.619 --> 23:34.621
I'm the one that should be thanking you.

23:34.704 --> 23:35.580
[inhales sharply]

23:36.289 --> 23:38.458
You're teaching me
what youth is all about.

23:40.961 --> 23:41.878
This is…

23:43.964 --> 23:44.798
flex!

23:46.466 --> 23:47.467
Right?

23:47.551 --> 23:48.718
[chuckles] Yes.

23:49.386 --> 23:50.637
[both laughing]

23:53.682 --> 23:55.559
- [Gang-yong] Let's take a look over there.
- Here?

23:55.642 --> 23:57.394
- No, no. Next to it.
- Oh, all right.

23:58.019 --> 23:59.396
[suspenseful music playing]

24:04.151 --> 24:05.152
[sighs]

24:14.119 --> 24:16.288
- How about up there? That part.
- Oh, all right.

24:30.969 --> 24:32.304
- All right. Thank you.
- Okay.

24:32.387 --> 24:33.472
[Gang-yong] Good job.

24:42.814 --> 24:44.065
[cell phone ringing]

24:47.319 --> 24:48.487
GANG-YONG

24:50.572 --> 24:52.824
- Yes.
- Onyu-ro 88.

24:53.909 --> 24:54.784
Will that do?

24:55.827 --> 24:57.078
Thank you very much.

25:00.332 --> 25:01.166
[exhales deeply]

25:01.666 --> 25:02.876
[music intensifies]

25:08.298 --> 25:10.008
- Let's go.
- Yes, sir!

25:10.509 --> 25:11.927
[tense music playing]

25:26.733 --> 25:28.568
[tires screeching]

26:12.487 --> 26:13.780
[music fades]

26:16.533 --> 26:17.367
[exhales]

26:18.034 --> 26:19.452
[suspenseful music playing]

26:24.416 --> 26:25.417
Look.

26:28.211 --> 26:29.212
[chuckles]

26:29.963 --> 26:31.631
President Choi is on crutches.

26:32.132 --> 26:33.758
[laughing]

26:45.228 --> 26:46.104
Hm.

26:46.938 --> 26:48.273
They tortured him.

26:50.609 --> 26:51.776
Did he rat us out?

26:52.444 --> 26:53.737
I'm not sure, sir.

26:54.738 --> 26:55.655
Hm.

26:56.615 --> 26:58.867
It's much safer for us to assume he did.

26:59.367 --> 27:01.870
- [exhales]
- Let's get President Choi.

27:04.289 --> 27:05.332
Then Jang-do.

27:06.416 --> 27:07.542
Yes, sir.

27:07.626 --> 27:08.585
[chuckles softly]

27:12.130 --> 27:13.214
Um, sir.

27:18.887 --> 27:21.056
LEE DU-YEONG

27:21.139 --> 27:23.141
[tense music playing]

27:29.606 --> 27:31.733
Make sure you don't kill the guy.

27:32.609 --> 27:34.027
I need information.

27:34.110 --> 27:34.944
Yes, sir.

27:35.612 --> 27:37.906
- And take off that thing.
- Oh.

27:40.075 --> 27:40.950
Mm.

27:51.670 --> 27:52.712
[music ends]

27:52.796 --> 27:53.713
[knocking at door]

27:56.508 --> 27:57.592
[knocking continues]

28:00.637 --> 28:02.097
[breathing deeply]

28:05.934 --> 28:06.768
[knocking]

28:07.727 --> 28:08.895
Honey.

28:10.230 --> 28:11.940
Someone's at the door.

28:12.524 --> 28:13.566
[knocking at door]

28:15.193 --> 28:16.403
[exhales deeply]

28:24.994 --> 28:26.204
[knocking]

28:28.081 --> 28:29.249
Who is it?

28:29.332 --> 28:30.625
[man] Uh, I'm from downstairs.

28:30.709 --> 28:33.461
I'm here because there's water leaking
from our ceiling.

28:33.962 --> 28:36.464
Would you mind
if I came in to check your bathroom?

28:39.342 --> 28:40.176
[sighs]

28:40.260 --> 28:41.720
I promise this won't take long.

28:41.803 --> 28:43.555
It's just
that our house is flooded right now.

28:44.681 --> 28:47.142
Our kids haven't gotten any sleep
because of this.

28:48.727 --> 28:50.311
I would really appreciate it.

28:51.563 --> 28:52.522
[groans]

28:53.565 --> 28:54.482
Right now?

28:54.566 --> 28:56.109
[man] Yes, it won't take long.

28:56.943 --> 28:58.445
I'll just check your bathroom.

29:04.200 --> 29:05.034
[grunts]

29:07.287 --> 29:08.204
[lock clicks]

29:12.125 --> 29:14.586
- [Du-yeong] Honey?
- Hm?

29:17.172 --> 29:19.841
- Who is it?
- He says water is leaking downstairs.

29:23.428 --> 29:24.512
- Move over, honey.
- Huh?

29:24.596 --> 29:25.430
[Du-yeong] Move over.

29:30.560 --> 29:31.603
Shh.

29:32.520 --> 29:33.396
[woman] Huh?

29:39.194 --> 29:40.445
- Just a second.
- Okay.

29:55.251 --> 29:59.047
Listen to me.
Call the cops now and report a burglary.

29:59.130 --> 30:02.300
- [shaky breathing] Why?
- I'll explain later.

30:03.176 --> 30:04.177
You trust me, right?

30:05.094 --> 30:05.929
Yes.

30:06.012 --> 30:07.263
And also,

30:07.889 --> 30:09.015
no matter what,

30:10.558 --> 30:12.268
do not open the door, you hear me?

30:12.352 --> 30:13.978
[whimpering] Okay.

30:15.563 --> 30:16.523
Mm-hm.

30:16.606 --> 30:18.775
[chuckles] It's all right, honey.

30:18.858 --> 30:20.985
Nothing's going to happen. It's all right.

30:21.069 --> 30:22.737
- [woman sobbing]
- [exhales deeply]

30:25.281 --> 30:26.199
Okay.

30:38.628 --> 30:40.839
- [inhales sharply]
- [tense music playing]

30:43.925 --> 30:44.843
[grunting]

30:51.182 --> 30:52.392
Dongjak-gu, Samjin-dong.

30:53.434 --> 30:54.269
[grunts]

31:03.486 --> 31:05.154
[grunting]

31:06.698 --> 31:08.283
Please, please!

31:08.366 --> 31:10.159
Hurry. My husband's in danger.

31:14.581 --> 31:16.207
[grunting]

31:16.291 --> 31:17.500
[screams]

31:21.504 --> 31:24.048
- [goon 1] Come on, come on. Let's go.
- [goon 2] Get in there. Go.

31:24.132 --> 31:25.842
- [broken glass falls]
- [goon 1] Where is he?

31:28.386 --> 31:29.429
- [grunts]
- [groans]

31:31.306 --> 31:33.933
- [grunts]
- Whoa! Shit.

31:34.017 --> 31:36.185
[goon 3] Go, go, go! Go!

31:38.229 --> 31:39.856
[all grunting]

31:45.028 --> 31:45.987
[goon 4 screams]

31:48.656 --> 31:50.116
[goon 5 screaming]

31:56.706 --> 31:58.625
- [goon 6 grunting]
- [Du-yeong groaning]

32:00.084 --> 32:02.378
- [screaming]
- [Du-yeong groans]

32:06.299 --> 32:07.342
[groans]

32:07.926 --> 32:09.844
- [goons grunting]
- [Du-yeong groaning]

32:12.263 --> 32:13.806
[crying]

32:15.099 --> 32:16.559
[all grunting]

32:17.518 --> 32:18.645
[goon screams]

32:24.317 --> 32:27.153
[grunting]

32:47.256 --> 32:48.549
[groans]

32:48.633 --> 32:49.926
[ragged breathing]

32:50.009 --> 32:51.636
[groaning]

32:52.887 --> 32:54.263
[crying]

33:15.576 --> 33:16.536
Hm.

33:17.745 --> 33:18.579
[music ends]

33:18.663 --> 33:19.580
[Du-yeong exhales]

33:21.708 --> 33:23.626
Tell me where to find Hwang Yang-jung,

33:25.128 --> 33:26.671
and I'll let your girl live.

33:31.342 --> 33:32.760
I always keep my promises

33:34.012 --> 33:35.096
with no exceptions.

33:38.016 --> 33:39.392
[inhales shallowly]

33:41.686 --> 33:42.687
Trust me.

33:52.113 --> 33:53.740
[whimpering]

33:55.491 --> 33:56.659
[whimpering]

33:58.995 --> 33:59.912
[sniffles]

34:00.997 --> 34:03.332
[Du-yeong continues whimpering]

34:08.629 --> 34:09.505
[sniffles]

34:13.301 --> 34:15.428
- [Gun-woo] Did you sleep well, Mr. Choi?
- I did.

34:16.596 --> 34:17.722
[Gun-woo] Did you sleep well?

34:17.805 --> 34:19.557
- Like a baby.
- [chuckles] Me too.

34:22.060 --> 34:23.436
[Mr. Choi] Hey, sit down.

34:26.314 --> 34:28.274
Hey, so this is a first for us.

34:28.900 --> 34:30.985
- Yes, we should do this more.
- [laughs]

34:32.361 --> 34:34.197
Dude, get up now. Hm.

34:34.280 --> 34:35.239
Let's eat.

34:38.367 --> 34:40.787
- Oh, wow. Thank you.
- [So-yeon] Oh, of course.

34:40.870 --> 34:43.206
- [Gun-woo] Mm. Yeah.
- Here.

34:43.289 --> 34:45.208
- He's not coming?
- He won't get up.

34:45.291 --> 34:47.668
God, you should've told him to eat
and then sleep.

34:47.752 --> 34:49.629
He got his fill last night, didn't he?

34:49.712 --> 34:50.922
- Yes.
- [Mr. Choi laughs]

34:51.005 --> 34:53.132
All that big talk
about being a good drinker.

34:53.216 --> 34:54.634
- [laughing]
- [Gun-woo chuckles]

34:54.717 --> 34:56.302
- Then let's eat.
- [Gun-woo] Thank you.

34:56.385 --> 34:58.471
- Thank you for this meal.
- Please enjoy.

35:02.100 --> 35:03.518
- [Mr. Choi exhales]
- [So-yeon laughs]

35:05.812 --> 35:06.854
Whoa!

35:07.897 --> 35:11.067
- Mm. Um, Gun-woo.
- Yes, sir?

35:11.150 --> 35:13.361
When are you taking your mother
to the orphanage?

35:14.153 --> 35:16.531
I can do it.
Let me borrow your car, Grandpa.

35:16.614 --> 35:18.449
It's been outside for a while.

35:18.533 --> 35:20.076
Someone might've seen it, so be careful.

35:20.159 --> 35:21.619
- I'll be okay.
- [Mr. Choi] All right.

35:21.702 --> 35:22.870
Do you wanna go after we eat?

35:22.954 --> 35:24.956
This time of day,
we should make it there in an hour.

35:26.624 --> 35:27.542
Mom, that work for you?

35:27.625 --> 35:29.252
Uh, to be honest,

35:29.752 --> 35:32.213
I think I… I would feel a lot better

35:32.296 --> 35:34.715
if I just stayed here
and kept preparing meals for everyone.

35:34.799 --> 35:36.342
[chuckles]

35:37.552 --> 35:38.469
Mrs. Yoon.

35:38.970 --> 35:39.804
[smacks lips]

35:40.304 --> 35:42.348
Uh, I don't mean to impose,

35:43.099 --> 35:45.476
but would you mind helping out
at our orphanage?

35:47.395 --> 35:50.481
It's just that
your cooking skills are really impressive…

35:50.565 --> 35:52.316
I think the children would love it.

35:53.609 --> 35:54.485
[exhales sharply]

35:54.569 --> 35:57.029
Mrs. Yoon, this food is just amazing.

35:57.113 --> 35:58.156
[Mr. Choi laughs]

36:01.242 --> 36:03.244
Mom, I also think
that would be for the best.

36:03.870 --> 36:06.539
[So-yeon inhales sharply, exhales deeply]

36:07.999 --> 36:11.961
- Well, okay if it helps you in any way.
- That's great. Thank you so much.

36:12.044 --> 36:13.254
[Mr. Choi and Yang-jung laugh]

36:13.337 --> 36:14.172
Yes.

36:14.714 --> 36:16.174
[gentle piano music playing]

36:18.843 --> 36:20.386
[breathes deeply]

36:23.181 --> 36:24.265
[Gun-woo sighs]

36:26.893 --> 36:30.688
So you're not going to be skipping meals,
you promise?

36:31.772 --> 36:32.607
Mm-hm.

36:38.279 --> 36:39.155
[So-yeon exhales]

36:40.281 --> 36:41.782
Please stay safe, sweetie.

36:43.784 --> 36:44.619
Mm-hm.

36:47.455 --> 36:48.414
[So-yeon exhales deeply]

36:50.416 --> 36:51.584
Don't worry so much, okay?

36:52.168 --> 36:53.002
Mm.

36:54.962 --> 36:56.672
I won't. I believe in my son.

36:56.756 --> 36:58.007
[chuckles]

37:08.184 --> 37:09.435
[engine revs]

37:13.397 --> 37:14.315
[music ends]

37:18.236 --> 37:21.030
HWANGSUSA

37:30.039 --> 37:31.916
SECURITY DISABLED

37:36.003 --> 37:36.879
Min-dong.

37:39.006 --> 37:41.008
[ominous music playing]

38:13.374 --> 38:15.376
[knife sharpening]

38:20.131 --> 38:21.424
[tense music playing]

38:28.180 --> 38:29.348
How did you find me?

38:30.558 --> 38:31.475
Well,

38:32.685 --> 38:34.520
Lee Du-yeong told me.

38:37.398 --> 38:39.275
Did you do something to his girl?

38:39.900 --> 38:40.818
Whoa, whoa.

38:43.612 --> 38:44.655
You kill them?

38:45.239 --> 38:46.240
[chuckles softly]

38:49.076 --> 38:50.244
[exhales sharply]

39:11.390 --> 39:12.516
[tea kettle whistling]

39:17.313 --> 39:18.606
[Myeong-gil grunts]

39:19.482 --> 39:20.649
[both grunting]

39:24.153 --> 39:25.279
[whistling continues]

39:39.251 --> 39:41.170
[both grunting]

39:42.129 --> 39:43.547
[Yang-jung exhales sharply]

39:45.257 --> 39:47.051
[both grunting]

39:48.427 --> 39:49.470
[Myeong-gil groans]

40:01.941 --> 40:03.067
[both grunting]

40:10.116 --> 40:11.283
[music fading]

40:11.367 --> 40:12.201
[groans]

40:13.494 --> 40:14.703
[groans]

40:14.787 --> 40:16.455
[Yang-jung breathing heavily]

40:28.634 --> 40:29.468
[music building]

40:32.054 --> 40:33.889
- [Yang-jung grunts]
- [Myeong-gil groans]

40:35.099 --> 40:36.684
[Myeong-gil grunting]

40:39.228 --> 40:40.354
[Myeong-gil screams]

40:41.772 --> 40:42.982
[groans]

40:44.108 --> 40:44.942
[shouts]

40:45.025 --> 40:46.694
[grunting]

40:50.614 --> 40:51.532
[Yang-jung grunts]

40:52.408 --> 40:54.326
[Myeong-gil groaning]

40:55.286 --> 40:57.037
- [music intensifies]
- [Myeong-gil screaming]

40:57.663 --> 40:58.873
[groaning]

40:59.707 --> 41:01.667
[both grunting]

41:17.391 --> 41:19.268
[Yang-jung panting]

41:20.436 --> 41:22.021
[both grunting]

41:25.441 --> 41:26.358
[groans]

41:30.362 --> 41:32.072
- [Myeong-gil grunts]
- [groans]

41:33.449 --> 41:35.034
[panting]

41:38.787 --> 41:40.080
[groaning]

41:46.212 --> 41:48.506
[Myeong-gil grunting]

41:53.761 --> 41:55.763
[Yang-jung groaning]

42:03.354 --> 42:05.064
[dramatic music playing]

42:05.898 --> 42:07.149
[groaning]

42:24.041 --> 42:24.917
[music ends]

42:46.397 --> 42:48.399
[tense music playing]

42:51.527 --> 42:52.570
[grunting]

42:53.988 --> 42:54.822
[grunts]

43:03.122 --> 43:04.415
[metal clanking]

43:17.386 --> 43:19.013
[music intensifies]

43:26.937 --> 43:27.771
Let's go.

43:30.816 --> 43:31.942
Come on. Go.

43:36.238 --> 43:37.615
[ominous music playing]

43:44.455 --> 43:45.539
[tense music playing]

43:50.544 --> 43:51.879
[panting] Mr. Choi!

43:52.463 --> 43:54.131
Kim Myeong-gil's thugs are outside.

43:54.214 --> 43:56.175
- What are you talking about?
- [exhales deeply]

43:58.636 --> 43:59.511
[Mr. Choi gasps]

44:04.224 --> 44:06.518
Let's go to the basement.
There's a gun down there.

44:18.781 --> 44:20.824
I'll stay behind.
Hurry up and go get the gun.

44:20.908 --> 44:22.326
- Go!
- No, Woo-jin!

44:22.951 --> 44:25.162
- [Woo-jin] Damn it!
- [Mr. Choi] Woo-jin, get out of there.

44:25.245 --> 44:26.872
Woo-jin!

44:26.955 --> 44:29.249
[Woo-jin grunting]

44:30.584 --> 44:31.585
[goon 1] Get in there.

44:31.669 --> 44:32.544
[screaming]

44:33.962 --> 44:35.130
No!

44:35.714 --> 44:37.591
- [goon 2] Go fuck him up!
- [Woo-jin grunts]

44:37.675 --> 44:39.009
[Mr. Choi] Woo-jin!

44:41.178 --> 44:42.179
[goon 3] Go, go, go!

44:43.681 --> 44:45.099
[uptempo rock music playing]

44:46.308 --> 44:47.726
[goons yelling indistinctly]

44:50.521 --> 44:51.563
[Woo-jin grunts]

44:53.607 --> 44:55.109
[goon 4] You're dead, motherfucker!

44:55.984 --> 44:56.819
[Woo-jin shouts]

44:58.529 --> 44:59.822
[panting]

45:04.451 --> 45:07.746
- [Woo-jin grunts]
- [goon 5] Let's get him.

45:07.830 --> 45:09.039
[groans]

45:09.123 --> 45:10.416
- [Woo-jin grunts]
- [shouts]

45:14.628 --> 45:15.629
[shouts]

45:17.923 --> 45:19.133
[Woo-jin grunting]

45:20.926 --> 45:22.052
[goon 6] Get in there!

45:23.429 --> 45:26.098
[screaming]

45:30.018 --> 45:31.019
[In-beom] Out of the way!

45:32.187 --> 45:33.564
[In-beom shouts]

45:38.318 --> 45:39.737
[groans]

45:44.575 --> 45:46.785
[Woo-jin groaning]

45:54.501 --> 45:55.836
[screams]

46:02.718 --> 46:04.470
[both grunting]

46:09.808 --> 46:10.684
[Woo-jin groans]

46:11.310 --> 46:12.269
[Woo-jin grunts]

46:20.277 --> 46:22.070
- [Woo-jin shouts]
- [groans]

46:22.613 --> 46:24.323
[shouting]

46:24.406 --> 46:25.365
[groans]

46:36.210 --> 46:37.377
[exhales sharply]

46:38.170 --> 46:39.505
- [grunts]
- [Woo-jin groans]

46:40.005 --> 46:41.465
[both grunting]

46:43.467 --> 46:45.427
[both grunting]

46:58.690 --> 46:59.650
[Woo-jin grunts]

47:03.612 --> 47:05.113
- [Woo-jin grunting]
- [groaning]

47:06.865 --> 47:09.117
Woo-jin! Woo-jin!

47:14.122 --> 47:14.957
[man grunting]

47:18.252 --> 47:19.545
[Woo-jin groaning]

47:22.297 --> 47:23.382
[blood splatters]

47:26.510 --> 47:27.845
Woo-jin!

47:36.520 --> 47:38.021
- [goon 7 screams]
- [gun fires]

47:41.191 --> 47:42.943
- [In-beom grunts]
- [Mr. Choi groans]

47:46.405 --> 47:48.156
[grunting]

47:48.866 --> 47:50.284
[In-beom grunts]

47:54.872 --> 47:57.374
- [In-beom grunting]
- [Mr. Choi groaning]

47:58.876 --> 48:00.168
[In-beom shouts]

48:01.295 --> 48:03.297
[screaming]

48:06.133 --> 48:07.050
[groans]

48:07.134 --> 48:10.137
[strained breathing]

48:10.971 --> 48:13.473
[Mr. Choi moaning]

48:14.057 --> 48:14.892
[goon 8] Sir.

48:14.975 --> 48:15.934
[goon 9 groaning]

48:17.603 --> 48:19.688
- [Myeong-gil] Where is he?
- This way, sir.

48:20.188 --> 48:21.023
Get pouring, you two.

48:21.106 --> 48:22.608
- [goon 10] Yes, sir.
- [goon 11] Yes, sir.

48:23.567 --> 48:25.068
[goon 12] groaning

48:26.236 --> 48:27.321
[Mr. Choi shallow breathing]

48:28.906 --> 48:30.240
Blood, ugh.

48:39.166 --> 48:40.250
[Myeong-gil scoffs]

48:44.796 --> 48:45.714
[In-beom sighs]

48:46.715 --> 48:47.633
Well done.

48:48.133 --> 48:49.009
[In-beom exhales]

48:51.845 --> 48:52.804
[Myeong-gil grunts]

48:55.641 --> 48:56.850
You are actually…

48:58.852 --> 49:00.354
someone I'm grateful for.

49:00.437 --> 49:01.813
- Hey, over here.
- [groaning]

49:04.274 --> 49:05.192
You see,

49:06.193 --> 49:07.986
you gave me a dream. [chuckles]

49:08.070 --> 49:10.113
[raspy breathing] You…

49:13.367 --> 49:14.242
[Mr. Choi grunts]

49:14.326 --> 49:16.495
That's why…

49:16.578 --> 49:18.163
- [strained breathing]
- [ominous music playing]

49:18.956 --> 49:20.624
…I'm going to make this painless.

49:21.500 --> 49:22.709
Oh, it's all right.

49:24.252 --> 49:27.005
It'll be over quick. It's all right.
You won't feel anything.

49:27.673 --> 49:29.049
- [knife stabs]
- Yeah, there.

49:29.132 --> 49:30.467
[Mr. Choi muffled moaning]

49:34.054 --> 49:36.098
It's all right. Ah, it's all right.

49:36.723 --> 49:37.557
[sighs]

49:53.448 --> 49:54.449
[Myeong-gil grunts]

50:02.332 --> 50:03.166
Mm.

50:05.919 --> 50:07.295
[music building]

50:11.925 --> 50:12.759
[music ends]

50:12.843 --> 50:14.428
[engine revs]

50:18.223 --> 50:19.850
[dramatic music playing]

50:19.933 --> 50:21.184
Gun-woo.

50:24.855 --> 50:26.857
- [engine revs]
- [tires screech]

50:28.734 --> 50:31.445
[both panting]

50:36.825 --> 50:38.243
- Try the back door.
- Okay.

50:42.247 --> 50:43.415
- [skin sizzles]
- [yells]

50:43.498 --> 50:45.000
[heavy breathing]

50:46.460 --> 50:47.961
[somber music playing]

50:48.837 --> 50:49.921
[grunts]

50:50.005 --> 50:51.339
[panting]

50:51.423 --> 50:52.466
Woo-jin!

50:52.966 --> 50:54.259
[shouts]

50:57.054 --> 50:58.847
[coughing]

51:04.102 --> 51:05.062
[Gun-woo grunting]

51:06.063 --> 51:06.897
No!

51:06.980 --> 51:08.899
[Gun-woo grunting]

51:10.776 --> 51:12.360
[grunting]

51:16.782 --> 51:19.409
[Gun-woo coughing, grunting]

51:22.162 --> 51:23.789
[Gun-woo panting]

51:35.258 --> 51:36.384
Hyeon-ju!

51:37.636 --> 51:39.096
Jesus, Hyeon-ju!

51:39.179 --> 51:40.680
[whimpering]

51:44.017 --> 51:45.102
Just hold on.

51:47.354 --> 51:48.188
Grandpa.

51:51.733 --> 51:52.567
Grandpa.

51:53.068 --> 51:56.446
Grandpa! Grandpa! [whimpers]

51:56.530 --> 51:58.865
Oh God, Grandpa.

51:58.949 --> 52:01.284
[whimpering] Grandpa!

52:03.954 --> 52:06.414
[wailing] Get up, please. You're not dead.

52:07.124 --> 52:08.917
[crying]

52:11.253 --> 52:14.589
Oh God! No, no! Gun-woo!

52:14.673 --> 52:16.716
[crying continues]

52:16.800 --> 52:19.052
Gun-woo, come! Gun-woo!

52:20.178 --> 52:22.389
Grandpa, please get up.

52:23.056 --> 52:26.560
Please, please help. Please, please.

52:28.770 --> 52:30.647
- [Gun-woo shallow breathing]
- Grandpa.

52:30.730 --> 52:32.691
- We need to get out, Hyeon-ju.
- No!

52:32.774 --> 52:35.277
- We have to get out! Hurry!
- No, no. We can't! Let go!

52:35.360 --> 52:37.028
If you stay here, you'll die too!

52:37.529 --> 52:40.031
Grandpa! Grandpa!

52:40.115 --> 52:41.658
- Let go of me!
- [grunts]

52:41.741 --> 52:43.076
[Hyeon-ju crying]

52:57.841 --> 52:59.134
[machines beeping]

52:59.885 --> 53:00.802
[surgeon] Scalpel.

53:03.972 --> 53:05.849
Suction! Some more gauze, please.

53:12.022 --> 53:14.191
- What's the patient's status?
- [anesthetist 1] BP's 80/50!

53:14.274 --> 53:15.317
Starting blood transfusion!

53:15.400 --> 53:18.236
We're short on blood because of COVID.
We'll need to get it elsewhere.

53:18.320 --> 53:20.030
Get us as much as you can somehow.

53:20.113 --> 53:21.156
Clip!

53:27.996 --> 53:29.080
[Hyeon-ju whimpering]

53:29.164 --> 53:31.374
- Then what do we do?
- His other legal guardian--

53:31.458 --> 53:32.417
[Gun-woo] What is it?

53:32.500 --> 53:34.502
They're saying
they don't have enough blood for Woo-jin.

53:34.586 --> 53:36.171
- Oh, God.
- What's your blood type?

53:36.254 --> 53:39.049
- [splutters] It's Type A.
- Come with me.

53:39.132 --> 53:40.425
[crying]

53:42.177 --> 53:45.180
I promise I'll save Woo-jin
no matter what, so don't worry. Okay?

53:45.263 --> 53:46.806
[whimpering] Okay.

53:56.274 --> 53:57.609
[exhales deeply]

53:57.692 --> 53:58.777
[machine beeps]

53:59.653 --> 54:01.988
- [machine beeping rapidly]
- [surgeon] He's losing a lot of blood.

54:02.072 --> 54:04.449
Please, we need more blood now!

54:05.116 --> 54:06.076
We need more gauze.

54:06.701 --> 54:08.161
I need it now. Please hurry.

54:09.996 --> 54:10.997
[nurse] All done.

54:11.665 --> 54:13.541
Is this enough to save Hong Woo-jin?

54:13.625 --> 54:15.585
[nurse]
No, I think we'll need a couple more bags.

54:15.669 --> 54:16.503
Oh.

54:17.003 --> 54:19.172
Okay, then let me
just fill up another one please.

54:19.256 --> 54:21.466
We've already gotten too much.
More would put you at risk.

54:21.549 --> 54:24.761
Oh, don't worry about it. I'm a boxer.
It'll take more than this to kill me.

54:24.844 --> 54:26.638
- It's fine.
- I'm sorry. I can't

54:26.721 --> 54:29.474
Listen to me.
I really, really have to save him. Please.

54:29.557 --> 54:32.519
[sniffles]
Please just let me fill up another one.

54:32.602 --> 54:34.145
- Please, I'm begging you.
- I really can't.

54:34.229 --> 54:35.981
This won't kill me, really.

54:36.064 --> 54:39.985
[whimpering] Please,
I have to save Woo-jin.

54:40.068 --> 54:41.444
I have to save him. [sniffles]

54:41.528 --> 54:43.446
I really won't die.
Please, I'm begging you.

54:43.530 --> 54:46.324
I'm begging you. Please, please.

54:46.408 --> 54:47.993
[surgeon] I can't see due to the blood.

54:48.076 --> 54:49.369
- Suction!
- [doctor] Applying suction.

54:49.452 --> 54:52.414
[suregon] I can't control the bleeding.
Please prepare the Surgicel.

54:52.497 --> 54:54.249
[anesthetist 2] Surgicel ready.

54:54.332 --> 54:56.751
[surgeon] Keep it coming.
I'll be needing more.

54:56.835 --> 54:59.337
Blood pressure dropping.
Please hurry. Hurry!

55:04.259 --> 55:06.261
[gentle piano music playing]

56:46.486 --> 56:47.570
[music ends]
